<%# Locals: `user`. The navbar's always-visible avatar tile (gradient initials via
    `variant: :tile`), wrapped in a stable Turbo target so a successful profile update
    can Turbo-replace it in place (Issue #13) — a name/username change alters the visible
    initials, and this keeps the bar in sync without a full navigation.

    Scope: only the tile lives inside this span. The dropdown MENU contents (the @handle
    line and "Your profile" link) are intentionally NOT wrapped/refreshed here — they are
    hidden until the menu opens and self-heal on the next navigation; the always-visible
    tile is the element this issue is about. The unread-notifications dot also stays
    OUTSIDE this span (it tracks unread count, not the profile edit). %>
<span id="<%= dom_id(user, :nav_avatar) %>">
  <%= render "ui/avatar", user: user, variant: :tile, size: :nav %>
</span>
